#
# 11g's reply to `begin :1 := pyo_obj_t(42, 'hello'); end;` with an object bound
# IN OUT (#2463): the bind prompt, then TTI_RXD and the object's value in the
# native object cell it went out in -- the constructed toid, the TOP_LEVEL
# flags and the new image (42, 'hello') -- with no indicator behind it, then the
# status.
# Captured 2026-11-07 through tools/capture_proxy.py: an OCI 11.2 program
# (instant client 11.2, x86-64 Linux, the client charset AL32UTF8, the object
# cache on; OCIObjectNew, then OCIBindObject of an SQLT_NTY bind, called through
# ctypes) on Oracle 11g XE 11.2.0.2, a DEDICATED session, with a throwaway type
# PYO_OBJ_T (n NUMBER, s VARCHAR2(20)) dropped after. The TTC payload, without
# the packet's header, as `hexdump -C` output; the offset column and the |ascii|
# gutter are ignored by tests.replay.parse_hexdump.
00000000  0b 01 05 b0 01 00 00 00  00 00 01 00 00 00 00 00  |................|
